FC-BCR strengthening: activation variables, TF set cuts, improved DA and separation

Major LP formulation strengthening (Section 11.1 of research memo):
- Activation variables s_v for all nodes with counting constraint
  sum(x_e) = sum(s_v) - 1 (tree has k-1 edges for k vertices)
- No-leaf constraints x(delta(v)) >= 2*s_v for Steiner nodes
- Edge-vertex coupling x_e <= s_u, x_e <= s_v

New cut families:
- Non-singleton TF cuts (Section 11.3): x(delta(S)) >= 2*x_e for
  terminal-free sets with exact min-cut separation oracle
- Partition inequalities integrated into separation loop

Solver improvements:
- Tailing-off detection stops cut rounds when LP stalls
- Cut limiting (top 30 most violated per round)
- Improved dual ascent: saturates each terminal cut fully
- Branching properly bounded to arc variables only

Preprocessing:
- Relaxed SD test restriction on contracted-adjacent edges
- Iterative SD application

Results: C-series 13/20 -> 18/20 optimal
- c10: 128s timeout -> 1.8s optimal
- c15: 160s timeout -> 2.1s optimal
- c08: 136s timeout -> 61s optimal
- c14: 131s timeout -> 72s optimal
- c13: 179s timeout -> 169s optimal
